A||||6||Alex2004||Imediate stalling after 1st -2nd start up!?!||||4||
Z||000000||Alex2004||12-06-2001||09:47 PM||||On my 84 SE 2.5(of course) sometimes like on cold mornings and whenever it's been running for a while when i go to start it, it will stall imediatly...then i start it again and then push the gas (right after starting) then it will start up.  What is wrong here?  Also whenever i've been driving for a while and then shut it off (say i'm running into the store for something) then come back out it comes close to dying if i do not give it gas.  Anyone knows what needs to be done to fix this?  I've replaced the plug wires and fuel filter...plugs need to be replaced in the near future but i cannot figure out what's causing this...let me know!  THanks!<P>Alex..||||reg||4
Z||000001||JetroGT||12-06-2001||10:05 PM||||It could be the ignition modual under the cap. Or a weak coil. My GT shut off on me last week. But a little before that it was staling and mis-firing. I thought it was the modual or the fuel pump but it was the coil. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||12-06-2001||10:39 PM||||How hard is it to replace the coil...where is it located?  and how much do they usually run?  thanks for the info!!<P>Alex...||||reg||5
Z||000003||JetroGT||12-06-2001||10:44 PM||||You can test the coil with a multi-meter. I'm not sure what the resistance should be. Wait, I have a new GM coil now. I'll post back after I check it.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">   <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.||||reg||1
Z||000004||JetroGT||12-06-2001||11:17 PM||||The resistance should be very close to zero on both connections. My meter only reads to 3 decimel places. the modual to cap connector read .000 and the other one was 4 ohms. <P>This is the only pic I had of the 84 L4.<BR>Indy version.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coil.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex2004||12-06-2001||11:25 PM||||ok, but where is the coil at?  and what  does it look like?  thanks! <P>Alex..||||reg||1
Z||000006||JetroGT||12-06-2001||11:41 PM||||Just follow the middle plug wire from the cap to the coil. On the L4 it sits sideways.<P>Forget them meater readings I posted. I tested it the wrong way. Sorry about that.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coil_1.jpg">    <P>Left______middle____right<BR>nothing___3 ohms____8.35 K ohms<P><p>[This message has been edited by JetroGT (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
